 - (2026-05-03, commit-ai-insights_20260502) To avoid import cycles, define local types (CommitInfo) that mirror external types (git.Commit) rather than importing the external package. ActivityEnhancer takes []CommitInfo instead of []git.Commit to keep ai package independent.
 - (2026-05-03, repo_health_monitoring_20260503) Health data comes from the existing /api/projects endpoint (health field included in Project struct). No new API needed for Phase 2 frontend work.
 - (2026-05-03, repo_health_monitoring_20260503) Health status determination: clean (0 issues) = healthy, minor (>0 but low) = warning, significant = critical. Divergence counts both ahead+behind as total divergence.
 - (2026-05-03, repo_health_monitoring_20260503) GetStaleBranches uses git for-each-ref with committerdate; branch must have a commit to appear in the list. Empty repos have no branches.
+- (2026-05-05, platform-git-features_20260505) Git format strings with | as delimiter work well for parsing multiple fields. Use `git stash list --format=%H|%gd|%s|%an|%at` for structured output with multiple fields.
+- (2026-05-05, platform-git-features_20260505) Stash@{N} references must be parsed by stripping `stash@{` prefix and `}` suffix, not by using the raw `%(refname)` which includes the braces.
+- (2026-05-05, platform-git-features_20260505) Git branch operations in tests need to be run against a repo with at least one commit; empty repos reject branch operations.
 - (2026-05-04, dashboard_customization_20260503) Theme system using CSS custom properties on :root with JS override works well; store theme name in localStorage, set data-theme on html element to allow CSS selectors, add inline script in <head> to prevent flash of unstyled content.
 - (2026-05-04, dashboard_customization_20260503) CSS transitions on body/header/cards (0.2s ease) make theme switching feel polished; use transition on background-color and border-color properties specifically.
 - (2026-05-04, dashboard_customization_20260503) Keyboard shortcuts (Ctrl+T for theme toggle) enhance power users' workflow; attach to document-level keydown event, preventDefault on Ctrl combos.
